<title>BERMUDA: ADT seeks dismissal of Western's Tyco suit.</title>
<headline>ADT seeks dismissal of Western's Tyco suit.</headline>
<dateline>HAMILTON, Bermuda 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>ADT Ltd said it has asked the Supreme Court of Bermuda to dismiss the lawsuit filed in Bermuda by Westar Capital Inc, a unit of Western Resources Inc.</p>
<p>Western filed suit last week seeking an order requiring Tyco's acqusition of ADT to be structured to provide appraisal rights to ADT shareholders. Western is a major ADT shareholder.</p>
<p>ADT also said that its stated grounds for dismissal are that Western's lawsuit has no basis in law and is frivolous, vexatious and an abuse of the process of the Supreme Court of Bermuda.</p>
<p>The suit is an attempt by Western to try to destabilize ADT's agreed merger with Tyco, ADT said.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610)).</p>
